:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.w3schools.com/python/python_conditions.asp&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336132430&amp;usg=AOvVaw0qaw6ebAl9Lad-004jXvzO" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.w3schools.com/python/python_conditions.asp</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Control Flow Tools (Official Python Docs):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/controlflow.html%2523if-statements&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336132593&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hCtpTDqCxC8x6AoAh0t2h" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/controlflow.html%2523if-statements&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336132710&amp;usg=AOvVaw34pJprp4jV6WtzwYjdhHNf" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/controlflow.html#if-statements</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.8mcuuj9rasrl" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:17pt;font-weight:700">Week 2: </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;font-size:17pt;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">for</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Loops and Iteration</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">Loops allow you to repeat a block of code multiple times. This is incredibly powerful and saves you from writing the same code over and over. A </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">for</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">&nbsp;loop</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is used when you have a collection of items and you want to do something for </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">each item</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;in that collection. üîÑ</span></p><h3 id="h.j2dn47orj6d0" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Iterating Over a Sequence</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">The most common use of a </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">for</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;loop is to iterate over a sequence like a string or a list.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_uxuibgyt35j2-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Structure:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;It starts with </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">for</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, followed by a temporary variable name (you choose this name), the keyword </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">in</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, the sequence you want to loop through, and a colon </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Let's go through a list of fruits</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-fa