padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:13pt;font-weight:700">Module 3: Functions, Modules, and Error Handling</span></h3><h2 id="h.m944f92cvfbi" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:16pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></h2><h2 id="h.pweudrcnle4n" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 1: Defining and Calling Functions</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">This week, you'll learn how to write your own functions. </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Functions</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;are reusable blocks of code that perform a specific task. They are the most important tool for organizing your code and avoiding repetition, a principle known as </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></p><h3 id="h.le6zt9pr7h29" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">What is a Function?</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_oh6asb5qzrh0-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;A function is like a recipe. üìú You define the recipe once (the steps and ingredients), and then you can "call" it anytime you want to cook that dish, perhaps with slightly different ingredients each time.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The two main steps are:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_vjxgp8bddnqe-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Defining the function:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;This is where you write the recipe.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Calling the function:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;This is where you actually use the recipe to do something.</span></li></ol><h3 id="h.9yj8esa0a0g3" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Defining a Function</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">You define a function using the </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">def</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;keyword, followed by the function's name, parentheses </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, and a colon </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. The code inside the function must be indented.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;p