n><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">try...except</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">&nbsp;(Real Python):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python-exceptions/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336168843&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n_EoWN9-lia7bG8MSNJi9" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python-exceptions/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336168918&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Yyevg9XFSjl2dMtx3Q-UW" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://realpython.com/python-exceptions/</a></span></li></ul><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p class="title" id="h.eua4da8dfc9h" style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:26pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:26pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Module 4</span></p><h3 id="h.alphj1yi8fbq" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Module 4: Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) in Python</span></h3><h2 id="h.ms0vf2rw5ykc" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:16pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.2h0yx746o9pq" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 1: Introduction to OOP - Classes and Objects</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">This week, you'll learn a new way of thinking about and structuring your code. Instead of just writing functions that operate on data, </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;is about creating "objects" that bundle together both data and the functions that operate on that data.</span></p><h3 id="h.se6fzp8wb58f" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Why OOP?</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">As programs grow, managing separate variables and functions becomes messy. OOP helps you organize complex code into logical, reusable blueprints. This makes your code easier to design, debug, and scale.</span></p><h3 id="h.l117e55nw4ly" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Classes and Objects</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">These are the two core concepts of OOP.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_e002uxc6w5od-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Class:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">class</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is a </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">blueprint</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;for creating objects. It defines a set of attributes (data) and methods (functions) that all objects of that class will have.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Object (or Instance):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;An </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">object</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is a specific </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">instance</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;created from a class. It's the actual thing built from the blueprint, with its own unique data.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;A class is like the architectural blueprint for a house üìú. It specifies that every house built from it will have windows, doors, and a roof. An object is an actual, physical house üè† built from that blueprint. You can build many houses (objects) from the same blueprint (class), and each one can have different properties (e.g., a different color of paint).</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.n1553od8ft30" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Defining a Simple Class</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">You define a class using the </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">class</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;keyword. By convention, class names start with a capital letter (PascalCase).</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This defines the blueprint for a Dog.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># It doesn't do anything yet, but the blueprint exists.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Dog:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">pass</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># The 'pass' keyword is a placeholder for future code.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.v6kjhrq8o42k" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Creating an Object (Instantiation)</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">Creating an object from a class is called </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">instantiation</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. You do it by calling the class name as if it were a function.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Dog:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">pass</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Create two different Dog objects from the Dog class blueprint</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">dog1 = Dog()</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">dog2 = Dog()</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># You can check their types and see that they are unique objects</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(</span><span style="color:#1967d2;font-size:10.5pt">type</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">(dog1)) &nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: &lt;class '__main__.Dog'&gt;</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(dog1) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: &lt;__main__.Dog object at 0x...&gt; (a unique memory address)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(dog2) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: &lt;__main__.Dog object at 0x...&gt; (a different memory address)</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">dog1</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;and </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">dog2</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;are now two distinct "Dog" objects, ready to have their own data.</span></p><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.k885fepn9v6k" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Further Research</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_kqjkeok8qw95-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Classes (Official Python Docs):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/classes.html&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336172397&amp;usg=AOvVaw0W5n1h_H-9cX607Xoh1OPY" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/classes.html&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336172498&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MEmMB-oX0-0A0wjznDLA7" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/classes.html</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Thinking in Objects (Real Python):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python3-object-oriented-programming/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336172621&amp;usg=AOvVaw1NCuK-n6T2MXkpES0uKzfG" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python3-object-oriented-programming/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336172721&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XP1G65v1SmsZQmBZy7tDx" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://realpython.com/python3-object-oriented-programming/</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.arj79ngc1vea" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:17pt;font-weight:700">Week 2: Attributes and Methods (</span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;font-size:17pt;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:17pt;font-weight:700">&nbsp;and </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;font-size:17pt;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">Now that you can create a blueprint, let's add some details. Objects have </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">attributes</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;(data/variables) and </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">methods</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(behavior/functions).</span></p><h3 id="h.ypaxysne7qn5" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:13pt;font-weight:700">The </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;font-size:13pt;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Method (The Constructor)</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is a special method that is automatically called when you create a new object. Its job is to set up the object's initial state by assigning values to its attributes. It is also known as the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">constructor</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></p><h3 id="h.sjxelljff1im" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:13pt;font-weight:700">The </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;font-size:13pt;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Keyword</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">The </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;parameter is the most important and often most confusing part of OOP for beginners.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_b9gan7r7h9r4-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">What it is:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;</span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is a reference to the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">current object instance</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. It's how an object can refer to its own attributes and methods.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;When you say, "I am hungry," the word "I" refers to </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-style:italic">you</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">. When an object's method uses </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, it's referring to </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-style:italic">itself</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">. </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">self.name</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;means "my own name."</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.m4r2qns81g9e" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Putting It Together: Attributes and Methods</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_li99koweu52m-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Attributes:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;Variables that belong to an object. They are defined inside </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;using </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">self.attribute_name = value</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Methods:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;Functions that belong to an object. They are defined inside the class and </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">must have </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">&nbsp;as their first parameter</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Dog:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This is the constructor. It runs when a new Dog object is created.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># 'self' refers to the specific dog being created (e.g., fido or bella).</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">__init__</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, name, age):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># These are attributes. We are attaching the data to the object itself.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.name = name</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.age = age</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;has been created!"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This is a method. It defines a behavior for the Dog class.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># It needs 'self' to access the object's own attributes.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">bark</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;says Woof!"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">get_age</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">return</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;self.age</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Create two Dog instances. The __init__ method is called automatically for each.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">fido = Dog(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Fido"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">, </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">4</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">) &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># 'fido' is passed as 'self' to __init__</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">bella = Dog(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Bella"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">, </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">2</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">) &nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># 'bella' is passed as 'self' to __init__</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Call methods on each instance. Python automatically passes the object as 'self'.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">fido.bark() &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: Fido says Woof!</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">bella.bark() &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: Bella says Woof!</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Access attributes directly</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{fido.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;is </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{fido.get_age()}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;years old."</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">) </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: Fido is 4 years old.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.hxbi5atvt64u" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Further Research</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_cpsm1rye3pi8-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Instance Methods (Real Python):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://realpython.com/instance-class-and-static-methods-in-python/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336176950&amp;usg=AOvVaw3P9WU2bBNCeqIdZNM9A2Gp" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://realpython.com/instance-class-and-static-methods-in-python/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336177109&amp;usg=AOvVaw1lujDSCLyM532aA5YzROnO" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://realpython.com/instance-class-and-static-methods-in-python/</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Understanding </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">self</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">&nbsp;in Python (GeeksforGeeks):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/self-in-python-class/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336177260&amp;usg=AOvVaw1HHe796-NHhyO3c-fL_kZr" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/self-in-python-class/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336177350&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UTzdIBzb-orytHb5A7GD6" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/self-in-python-class/</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.mtdc2t1wugah" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 3: The Four Pillars - Encapsulation &amp; Abstraction</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The "Four Pillars of OOP" are core principles that guide the design of good object-oriented systems. This week, we'll cover the first two.</span></p><h3 id="h.7s99uvl9ju8d" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. Encapsulation</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Encapsulation</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;means bundling the data (attributes) and the methods that operate on that data into a single unit (the class). It also involves restricting direct access to an object's internal state.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_qtowkbp6uzoa-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;Think of a car's dashboard. You, the driver, interact with a simple interface (steering wheel, pedals). You don't directly manipulate the engine's fuel injectors or the transmission's gears. The car's complex inner workings are </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">encapsulated</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, and you're given a safe, simple interface to use it.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">In Python, we hint that an attribute should be "private" (not accessed directly from outside the class) by prefixing its name with an underscore </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">_</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">. This is a </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">convention</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, not a strict rule.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;BankAccount:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">__init__</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, initial_balance):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># By convention, '_' means this should not be changed directly from outside.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self._balance = initial_balance</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">deposit</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, amount):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">if</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;amount &gt; </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">0</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self._balance += amount</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"Deposited $</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{amount}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">. New balance: $</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self._balance}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">else</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Deposit amount must be positive."</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">get_balance</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">return</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;self._balance</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Good practice: Use the methods to interact with the data</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">my_account = BankAccount(</span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">100</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">my_account.deposit(</span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">50</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"Current balance: $</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{my_account.get_balance()}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Bad practice: Accessing the "private" attribute directly</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># my_account._balance = -500 # This breaks the logic of the object</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.pwtrss3wiek5" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">2. Abstraction</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Abstraction</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;means hiding the complex implementation details and showing only the essential features of the object. Encapsulation enables abstraction.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_gs9juiexukot-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;The TV remote control is a perfect example of abstraction. You press the "Volume Up" button. You don't need to know </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-style:italic">how</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;the remote sends the signal, how the TV receives it, or how the speaker's electronics increase the sound level. All that complexity is </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">abstracted</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;away, leaving you with a simple button.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">In our </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">BankAccount</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;example, </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">deposit()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is an abstraction. The user doesn't need to know how the balance is stored or updated; they just know they can call </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">deposit()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;with an amount.</span></p><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.mw27tzl9u0t6" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Further Research</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_gz8b8f4s1j1n-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Encapsulation in Python:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/encapsulation-in-python/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336180839&amp;usg=AOvVaw3a69F8dMT_SR_6ZP-l4RG9" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/encapsulation-in-python/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336180951&amp;usg=AOvVaw3UI7yO2xdM-gVLDs0hkYSQ" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/encapsulation-in-python/</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Abstraction in Python:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.askpython.com/python/oops/abstraction-in-python&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336181100&amp;usg=AOvVaw08jc5XOrWgaaNpydlaT3hb" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.askpython.com/python/oops/abstraction-in-python&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336181202&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tYri15HJa3Dwlw0EeYXtA" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.askpython.com/python/oops/abstraction-in-python</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.ebtgpuuzuxhs" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 4: The Four Pillars - Inheritance</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Inheritance</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is the mechanism that allows you to create a new class (the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">child class</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;or subclass) that inherits attributes and methods from an existing class (the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">parent class</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;or superclass).</span></p><h3 id="h.k6uzkvk28hp7" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Why Use Inheritance?</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">It promotes code reuse. You can create a general parent class and then create more specialized child classes that add new features or modify existing ones without rewriting the original code. This creates an "is a" relationship (e.g., a </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Dog</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;"is an" </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Animal</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">).</span></p><h3 id="h.qr1abbusresy" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">How to Implement Inheritance</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">You specify the parent class in parentheses after the child class name.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This is the Parent Class (or Superclass)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Animal:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">__init__</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, name):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.name = name</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">speak</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># A generic sound, because we don't know what kind of animal it is</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;makes a sound."</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This is a Child Class (or Subclass)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Dog inherits from Animal</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Dog(Animal):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">__init__</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, name, breed):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Call the parent's __init__ method to handle the 'name' attribute</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#1967d2;font-size:10.5pt">super</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">().__init__(name)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.breed = breed </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Add a new attribute specific to Dog</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># We can override the parent's 'speak' method</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">speak</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;barks!"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Another Child Class</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Cat(Animal):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This class doesn't have its own __init__, so it uses the parent's</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">pass</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># It will inherit everything from Animal without changes</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">my_dog = Dog(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Fido"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">, </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Golden Retriever"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">my_cat = Cat(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Whiskers"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">my_dog.speak() </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: Fido barks! (This uses the Dog's overridden method)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">my_cat.speak() </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output: Whiskers makes a sound. (This uses the Animal's original method)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(my_dog.breed) </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Child classes can have their own attributes</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><ul class="lst-kix_au37ogq71s96-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">super()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;The </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">super()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;function is a special function that allows a child class to call methods from its parent class. It's commonly used in </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;to ensure the parent's setup code is run.</span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.mtpyn8jgk9lz" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Further Research</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_c8f5ss7as022-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Inheritance in Python (Real Python):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://realpython.com/python-inheritance/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336184694&amp;usg=AOvVaw3amAJGpTtNSUtIqb1eMr2K" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://realpython.com/python-inheritance/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336184802&amp;usg=AOvVaw1EORuYXPR6XB9GxoEsfTyO" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://realpython.com/python-inheritance/</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">super()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">&nbsp;in Python (Real Python):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python-super/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336184919&amp;usg=AOvVaw0niLW858g5IP8_jfq3qyF3" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python-super/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336184994&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_UTCqvegGfo6wx0FYLE6v" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://realpython.com/python-super/</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.w5ktkwg41pro" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 5: The Four Pillars - Polymorphism</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Polymorphism</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, from Greek meaning "many forms," is the ability of different objects to respond to the same method call in different, class-specific ways.</span></p><h3 id="h.vlv3d2bdgyjs" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Understanding Polymorphism</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">Inheritance is one way to achieve polymorphism. In our previous example, both </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Dog</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;and </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Cat</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;objects could respond to a </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">.speak()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;call, but they did so differently.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The real power of polymorphism is that you can write code that works with objects of the parent class, and it will automatically work with any child class objects as well, without needing to know their specific type.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_uwaupwmn3qvl-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;You have a "play" button on a remote. If the remote is controlling a DVD player, "play" starts the movie. If it's controlling a CD player, "play" starts the music. The button is the same (</span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">.speak()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">), but the result depends on the object it's controlling (</span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Dog</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;or </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Cat</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">).</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Animal:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">__init__</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, name):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.name = name</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">speak</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">raise</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;NotImplementedError(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Subclass must implement this method"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Dog(Animal):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">speak</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">return</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;says Woof!"</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Cat(Animal):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">speak</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">return</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;says Meow!"</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Duck(Animal):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">speak</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">return</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{self.name}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;says Quack!"</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Create a list of different Animal objects</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">animals = [Dog(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Fido"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">), Cat(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Whiskers"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">), Duck(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"Donald"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)]</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This loop doesn't care what specific type of animal it has.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># It just knows that any Animal object should have a .speak() method.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># This is polymorphism in action!</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">for</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;animal </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">in</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;animals:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; print(animal.speak())</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Output:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Fido says Woof!</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Whiskers says Meow!</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Donald says Quack!</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.agw8rx5w1x23" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Further Research</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_bxdbq6e5iqrt-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Polymorphism in Python (GeeksforGeeks):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/polymorphism-in-python/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336188344&amp;usg=AOvVaw2qOTqo5cxKKmEUVmxjLPdW" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/polymorphism-in-python/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336188454&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ebJ3RwTCg_5c1b0KeyBVy" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/polymorphism-in-python/</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.pwyw75yp89e9" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 6: Magic Methods (Dunder Methods)</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Magic Methods</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, also known as </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Dunder Methods</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;(for </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">D</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">ouble </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Under</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">score), are special methods with double underscores at the beginning and end of their names (e.g., </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__str__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">). They allow your custom objects to integrate with Python's built-in syntax and functions.</span></p><h3 id="h.qv1gs72uw56" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Why are they "magic"?</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">They are rarely called directly. Instead, Python calls them automatically in response to specific actions. For example, Python calls </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__init__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;when you create an object and </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">__add__</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;when you use the </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">+</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;operator.</span></p><h3 id="h.kmrg83gz9slu" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Common and Useful Dunder Methods</span></h3><ol class="lst-kix_sv4datgxszth-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">__str__(self)</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_sv4datgxszth-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">What it does:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;Defines what happens when you try to convert your object to a string, for example, when you </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">print()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;it. It should return a user-friendly string.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Without it:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;</span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">print(my_object)</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;shows a useless memory address.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">With it:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;</span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">print(my_object)</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;shows a nice, readable description.</span></li></ul><ol class="lst-kix_sv4datgxszth-0" start="2" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">__len__(self)</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_sv4datgxszth-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">What it does:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;Defines what happens when you call the built-in </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">len()</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;function on your object. It should return an integer.</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.pm92fgbzok62" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Example</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">Let's build a </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">Book</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;class that uses these methods.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">class</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;Book:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">__init__</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(self, title, author, pages):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.title = title</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.author = author</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; self.pages = pages</s