:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">A </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">hash table</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;(or hash map) is a data structure that implements an associative array abstract data type, a structure that can map </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">keys</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;to </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">values</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">. It is the underlying data structure for Python's </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">dictionaries</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></p><h3 id="h.z91e4nyc00mv" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">How do they work?</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">A hash table uses a </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">hash function</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;to compute an index (a "hash") into an array of buckets or slots, from which the desired value can be found.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_1itli9wf8003-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A hash table is like a magical, super-efficient filing cabinet üóÑÔ∏è. When you want to store a file (the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">value</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">), you give it a unique label (the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">key</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">). The librarian (the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">hash function</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">) instantly calculates which specific drawer (the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">index</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">) the file belongs in. To retrieve it, you just give the label, and the librarian knows exactly where to look without searching.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Key Properties:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_edoilux5qdix-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Time Complexity (Average Case):</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_edoilux5qdix-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Insertion:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;O(1)</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Deletion:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;O(1)</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Search/Access:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;O(1)</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_edoilux5qdix-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Worst Case:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;In the rare event of a "hash collision" (multiple keys hashing to the same index), the performance can degrade to O(n). Good hash functions make this unlikely.</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.6u2j3pvh9fa8" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python's Dictionary</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">You've been using hash tables all along! Python's </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">dict</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;is a highly optimized hash table implementation.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Creating a dictionary (hash table)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">user_ages = {</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"alice"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">: </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">30</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">, </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># "alice" is hashed to an index where 30 is stored</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"bob"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">: </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">25</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">,</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"charlie"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">: </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">35</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">}</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Accessing a value (average O(1))</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(user_ages[</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"bob"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">]) </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># 25</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Inserting a value (average O(1))</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">user_ages[</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"david"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">] = </span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">28</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;line-height:1.15;backgrou