y:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.4ievao4hhgk3" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 7: Non-Linear Data Structures - Graphs</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">A </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">graph</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is a data structure used to represent connections or relationships between pairs of objects. It consists of a set of </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">vertices</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;(or nodes) and a set of </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">edges</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;that connect these vertices.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_vivqx7uel9fk-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A graph is like a map of cities and roads üó∫Ô∏è. The cities are the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">vertices</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">, and the roads connecting them are the </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">edges</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.6x4by1offd8n" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Terminology</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_lvgzkjm07scv-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Directed Graph:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Edges have a direction (like a one-way street).</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Undirected Graph:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Edges have no direction (like a two-way street).</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Weighted Graph:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Edges have a "weight" or "cost" associated with them (like the distance of a road).</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.b9x4pfokwhkf" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Representing a Graph</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">The most common way to represent a graph in code is using an </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">adjacency list</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. This is a dictionary where each key is a vertex, and its value is a list of the vertices it's connected to.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Representing an undirected graph of a social network</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># A is friends with B and C</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># B is friends with A and D</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># ...</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">social_network = {</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"A"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">: [</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"B"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">, </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"C"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">],</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"B"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">: [</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"A"</sp