</span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/depth-first-search-or-dfs-for-a-graph/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336319339&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PV9-0ktbJfURwdBCppvw0" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/depth-first-search-or-dfs-for-a-graph/</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Graph Traversal Visualization (VisuAlgo):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://visualgo.net/en/graphds&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336319460&amp;usg=AOvVaw32attxGpexuJuWWnL3Ji1f" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://visualgo.net/en/graphds&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336319523&amp;usg=AOvVaw33V3ytaTIhaHeqzc8cmhwp" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://visualgo.net/en/graphds</a></span></li></ul><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p class="title" id="h.tdk8snbncppc" style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:26pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:26pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Tab 11</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Of course. Here are the comprehensive notes for Module 11 on Concurrency and Parallelism, broken down into a 4-week schedule.</span></p><h2 id="h.jr2isbtnztiz" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 1: Concurrency vs. Parallelism &amp; The GIL</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">This week introduces the theoretical foundation for writing programs that can do more than one thing at a time. It's crucial to understand the difference between concurrency and parallelism.</span></p><h3 id="h.193ahwsfwq8j" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Concurrency vs. Parallelism</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">These two terms are often used interchangeably, but they mean different things.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_z1roa0sepvgk-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Concurrency:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A program is </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">concurrent</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;if it is </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">managing</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;multiple tasks at the same time. The tasks might not be running simultaneously, but the program is structured to switch between them.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_z1roa0sepvgk-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A single chef in a kitchen üßë‚Äçüç≥. The chef might start boiling water for pasta (a task that involves waiting), and while the water heats up, they switch to chopping vegetables. They are </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-style:italic">managing</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;both tasks at once, but only </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-style:italic">doing</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;one thing at any given instant.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_z1roa0sepvgk-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Parallelism:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A program is </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">parallel</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;if it is </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">executing</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;multiple tasks at the exact same time. This is only possible on a machine with multiple CPU cores.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_z1roa0sepvgk-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A kitchen with multiple chefs üßë‚Äçüç≥üßë‚Äçüç≥. One chef can be boiling pasta while another chef is chopping vegetables simultaneously. They are </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-style:italic">doing</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;multiple tasks in parallel.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">All parallel programs are concurrent, but not all concurrent programs are parallel.</span></p><h3 id="h.kg8s3zs20xgw" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">I/O-Bound vs. CPU-Bound Tasks</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Understanding what limits your task's speed is key to choosing the right concurrency model.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_hx6xhjxmva47-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">I/O-Bound Task:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;A task that spends most of its time </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">waiting</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;for something to happen. This "something" is often an Input/Output (I/O) operation, like a network request, a database query, or reading a large file from a disk. The CPU is mostly idle during these waits. Concurrency is perfect for this.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">CPU-Bound Task:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;A task that spends most of its time doing heavy computations. It's limited by the speed of the CPU. Examples include complex mathematical calculations, image processing, or video encoding. Parallelism is needed to speed these up.</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.ymalz9t6bk32" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Global Interpreter Lock (GIL)</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">This is a famous and often misunderstood part of CPython (the standard Python implementation).</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_wju2i7ydmkdk-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">What it is:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;The </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">GIL</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is a mutex (a type of lock) that protects access to Python objects, preventing multiple threads from executing Python bytecode </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">at the same time</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;within a single process.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">What it means:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;Even if you have a multi-core CPU, the GIL ensures that only </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">one thread</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;can be executing Python code at any given moment.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Impact:</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_wju2i7ydmkdk-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">It makes Python's memory management much simpler.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">It means </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">threading in Python cannot be used for true parallelism for CPU-bound tasks</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:30pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:72pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">It does </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">not</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;significantly impact </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">I/O-bound tasks</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, because the GIL is released by a thread while it's waiting for I/O, allowing other threads to run.</span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h3 id="h.tcjlnbwrgy0" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Further Research</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_dva3t4obzptg-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Concurrency vs. Parallelism (Video):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://www.youtube.com/watch%253Fv%253D10dgo99cltE&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336322997&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oSaJ2RFmeBB65hMQv2P2l" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/search?q%3Dhttps://www.youtube.com/watch%253Fv%253D10dgo99cltE&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336323107&amp;usg=AOvVaw28BISACDKY40bpnfT8A-1W" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=10dgo99cltE</a></span></li><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">What is the Python Global Interpreter Lock (GIL)? (Real Python):</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python-gil/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336323240&amp;usg=AOvVaw0R33bZwLsLdlzVbD77c2cv" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">&nbsp;</a></span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://realpython.com/python-gil/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786364336323309&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TW6N1cecsCs5Mtx2_OKLu" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">https://realpython.com/python-gil/</a></span></li></ul><hr><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><h2 id="h.5obobs5b1k6l" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:16pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:17pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Week 2: Threading</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Threading</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;is Python's primary tool for achieving </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">concurrency</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d">&nbsp;for </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">I/O-bound tasks</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. A thread is a lightweight, separate flow of execution. Multiple threads can exist within a single process and share the same memory space.</span></p><h3 id="h.9icikcn8a8s9" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">How Threading Works</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:6pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">You can create multiple threads and assign each one a task. The operating system will manage switching between these threads. When one thread is blocked waiting for an I/O operation (like fetching a URL), the Python GIL is released, and the OS can switch to another thread to do its work.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_6zkdvs73so2y-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding-top:0pt;color:#000000;padding-left:0pt;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:18pt;line-height:1.15;margin-right:0;margin-left:36pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;orphans:2;margin-bottom:0;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700">Analogy:</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The single chef (your program) has multiple hands (threads). The chef can use one hand to start boiling water. While that's happening and that hand is just waiting, they can use another hand to chop vegetables. The hands share the same workspace (memory).</span></li></ul><h3 id="h.tt222ez9thhq" style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#434343;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:6pt;line-height:1.15;page-break-after:avoid;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:13pt;font-weight:700">Using the </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;font-size:13pt;color:#575b5f;font-weight:700">threading</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:13pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Module</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#1b1c1d">Python's built-in </span><span style="background-color:#e9eef6;color:#575b5f">threading</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;module makes it easy to work with threads.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:14pt;line-height:1.15;background-color:#f0f4f9;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Python</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">import</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;threading</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">import</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;time</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">def</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#996900;font-size:10.5pt">download_site</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">(url):</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"Starting download for </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{url}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># time.sleep(3) simulates a 3-second network request</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; time.sleep(</span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">3</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"Finished download for </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{url}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># --- Sequential (No Threading) ---</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">start_time = time.time()</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">download_site(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"site_A"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">download_site(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"site_B"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">duration = time.time() - start_time</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">print(</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">f"Sequential run took </span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">{duration:</span><span style="color:#b55908;font-size:10.5pt">.2</span><span style="color:#1b1c1d;font-size:10.5pt">f}</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;seconds\n"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">) </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Will take ~6 seconds</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># --- Concurrent (With Threading) ---</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">sites = [</span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"site_A"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">, </span><span style="color:#188038;font-size:10.5pt">"site_B"</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">]</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">threads = []</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">start_time = time.time()</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">for</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;site </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">in</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;sites:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Create a thread. 'target' is the function to run. 'args' is a tuple of arguments.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; thread = threading.Thread(target=download_site, args=(site,))</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; threads.append(thread)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Start the thread's execution</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; thread.start()</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#5f6368;font-size:10.5pt"># Wait for all threads to complete before moving on</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">for</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-size:10.5pt">&nbsp;thread </span><span style="color:#8430ce;font-size:10.5pt">in</span><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;threads:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp; &nbsp; thread.join()</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#575b5f;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;orphans:2;widows:2;text-